    "body": "## Summary\n- add a reusable `UserTrustCard` backed exclusively by the existing public profile endpoint\n- show requester/worker reputation directly in job details instead of opaque numeric user IDs\n- show the selected counterpart's compact trust summary above chat history\n- include verification, rating/review count, completed-job total, public location, declared specializations, account age/bio where space permits, and a link to the full public profile\n- deduplicate concurrent profile reads and cache successful reads for the current browser session\n- degrade gracefully if public trust data cannot be loaded, without blocking job lifecycle or chat actions\n- document inline trust-card behavior and privacy boundaries\n\n## Product impact\nA prospective worker can review the requester's public reputation before accepting an open job. Once a job has a worker, both parties can inspect each other's trust signals from the job lifecycle screen. The chat keeps the same context visible while users communicate instead of forcing a separate profile lookup.\n\n## Privacy / safety\n- the cards consume only `GET /users/{id}/profile`; no new backend access surface is introduced\n- no email, exact job location, route geometry, live tracking, payment/escrow data, verification documents or moderation data is requested or rendered\n- a profile-read failure is fail-open for surrounding workflow: messaging, completion, disputes, cancellation and escrow-related controls remain usable\n- blocking semantics are unchanged; the card does not grant any new interaction capability\n\n## Validation\nRun frontend dependency audit/lint/build and the repository's selected CI/runtime smoke workflows. Do not merge unless the latest head is fully green.",
